# The runtime's own classes, as the --extern= table declares a .NET class
# (README, "External .NET classes"): row flag X, the RETTYPE its C# type
# name, then the members (`Class::member`, RETTYPE the member's type) and
# the methods (`Class::Class__Method`). Loaded after the reftab by the
# scan and the emitter, beside hbfuncs.tab, never saved. With a class
# here the name rule types a variable that names it (`oError` is an
# `Error`), a declaration can name it, and its members are typed.
#
# Error: Harbour's error object (ErrorNew(), a RECOVER USING variable,
# the WITH block's parameter), HbRuntime's HbError (HbRuntime.Errors.cs).
Error	X	HbError	0
Error::severity	-	NUMERIC	0
Error::genCode	-	NUMERIC	0
Error::subSystem	-	STRING	0
Error::subCode	-	NUMERIC	0
Error::description	-	STRING	0
Error::operation	-	STRING	0
Error::fileName	-	STRING	0
Error::osCode	-	NUMERIC	0
Error::tries	-	NUMERIC	0
Error::canRetry	-	LOGICAL	0
Error::canDefault	-	LOGICAL	0
Error::canSubstitute	-	LOGICAL	0
Error::args	-	-	0
Error::cargo	-	-	0
Error::Error__classname	-	STRING	0
